-- g8-tests-reg4.l4: regulation 4, payment of the fee as a condition of the licence, the exams and the objection.
--
-- Expected values, decided from the words of regulation 4 before any run:
--   the bar applies to a service "for which a fee was fixed under these regulations" and lapses once the payer "paid
--   the fee in full".  So: fee fixed and not paid in full -> barred; fee paid in full -> not barred; no fee fixed -> the
--   bar is not engaged (taken), or the answer is a refusal (alternative).
--   "In full": a payment of at least the fee (taken: overpayment is payment of the whole fee); only exactly the fee (alternative).
--   The first limb binds the Registrar (give a licence, renew it); the second the Training Division (allow an exam,
--   allow the lodging of an objection).
-- Days before 1 January 2026 are used wherever the printed figure is meant, so that no index reading is needed; one
-- group of tests uses the updated figure of 1.1.2026 (196 for a practical exam) with the illustrative readings of
-- g8-tests-reg3.l4, repeated here.

§ `Tests of regulation 4`

§§ `Names for the test data`

GIVETH A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
vM MEANS `the Fees Regulations as made`

GIVETH A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
vA MEANS `the Fees Regulations as amended`

GIVETH A `Vintage of the Fees Regulations`
vD MEANS `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations`

GIVETH A `Price index reading`
`the reading published on 15 June 2025` MEANS
    `Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2025, `month of the index` IS 5, `published on` IS YMD 2025 6 15, `value of the index` IS 100

GIVETH A `Price index reading`
`the reading published on 15 November 2025` MEANS
    `Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2025, `month of the index` IS 10, `published on` IS YMD 2025 11 15, `value of the index` IS 101.25

GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`the illustrative readings` MEANS
    LIST `the reading published on 15 June 2025`, `the reading published on 15 November 2025`

GIVEN readings IS A LIST OF `Price index reading`
GIVETH AN `Inputs of regulation 3`
taken readings MEANS
    `the inputs of regulation 3 under the reading the encoding takes, with the readings` readings

GIVETH A `Reading of regulation 4`
r4 MEANS `the reading of regulation 4 that the encoding takes`

§§ `The text as made: a practical exam, a fee of 194, both sides of the amount`

-- Before the first update day, so the printed figure.  Paid in full: 194 and more.  Not in full: 193 and less.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a practical exam` 194 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a practical exam` 193 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a practical exam` 0 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a practical exam` 400 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY

-- The bar itself, on the same facts.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, in` vM `for the service` `the service of sitting a practical exam` `, the payer having paid` 193 `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, in` vM `for the service` `the service of sitting a practical exam` `, the payer having paid` 194 `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY)

-- Alternative on "in full": only exactly the fee.  400 is then not payment in full; 194 still is; 193 still is not.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that wants exactly the fee`) `, in` vM `for the service` `the service of sitting a practical exam` `, the payer having paid` 400 `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that wants exactly the fee`) `, in` vM `for the service` `the service of sitting a practical exam` `, the payer having paid` 194 `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY)
#ASSERT `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that wants exactly the fee`) `, in` vM `for the service` `the service of sitting a practical exam` `, the payer having paid` 193 `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY)

§§ `The Training Division and the Registrar: which official, and a refusal for the wrong service`

#ASSERT `regulation 4 leaves the Training Division free to allow the exam or the objection in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a practical exam` 194 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 leaves the Training Division free to allow the exam or the objection in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a practical exam` 193 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT `regulation 4 leaves the Training Division free to allow the exam or the objection in the vintage` vM `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` 40 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 leaves the Training Division free to allow the exam or the objection in the vintage` vM `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` 39 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vM `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` 284 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vM `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` 283 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vM `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` 0 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY

#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a practical exam` 194 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY BECAUSE "regulation 4 binds the Registrar for licences only, and the service is not a licence"
#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 leaves the Training Division free to allow the exam or the objection in the vintage` vM `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` 284 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY BECAUSE "regulation 4 binds the Training Division for exams and objections only, and the service is neither"

-- Regulation 4 does not speak of an application for an ordinary licence, nor of a continuing training course.
#ASSERT `the official that regulation 4 binds for the service, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, the service` `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the official that regulation 4 binds for the service, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, the service` `the service of attending a continuing training course` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the official that regulation 4 binds for the service, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, the service` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST `the Registrar`
#ASSERT `the official that regulation 4 binds for the service, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, the service` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` EQUALS JUST `the Training Division`
#ASSERT `the official that regulation 4 binds for the service, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, the service` `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` EQUALS JUST `the Training Division`

§§ `A service for which no fee is fixed: the bar is not engaged (taken); the alternative refuses`

-- As made: no fee for a theoretical exam; as amended: none for an objection to a practical exam; none for a training course.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 0 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vA `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` 0 (YMD 2026 5 4) (`the illustrative readings`)
#ASSERT `regulation 4 leaves the Training Division free to allow the exam or the objection in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 0 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vM `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal` 0 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vM `the service of attending a continuing training course` 0 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY

-- The alternative: regulation 4 refuses to say about a service the text prices not at all.
#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that refuses where no fee is fixed`) `, in` vM `for the service` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` `, the payer having paid` 0 `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY) BECAUSE "regulation 4 speaks of a service for which a fee was fixed, and this text of the regulations fixes none for the service"
-- It does not refuse where a fee is fixed.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that refuses where no fee is fixed`) `, in` vM `for the service` `the service of sitting a practical exam` `, the payer having paid` 0 `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY)

