#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a practical exam` 196 (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "regulation 3(a) needs the index of a month, and no reading for that month was supplied"
-- But a silent head needs no reading: nothing is owed.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 0 (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY

§§ `A temporary licence: the fee is fixed for the application, the bar speaks of a licence for which a fee was fixed`

-- Taken: the fee fixed for the application binds the grant (the Registrar is the official for the application's service).
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vM `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` 0 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vM `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` 397 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY
#ASSERT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vM `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` 398 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY

-- Alternative: only a fee fixed for the licence itself binds its grant, and no text fixes one: not barred, whatever was paid.
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that binds a temporary licence only by a fee fixed for the licence`) `, in` vM `for the service` `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` `, the payer having paid` 0 `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY)
#ASSERT `the official that regulation 4 binds for the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that binds a temporary licence only by a fee fixed for the licence`) `, the service` `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` EQUALS NOTHING
-- THE GRANT ITSELF (the finding DIS-4 of the independent test author, which the first version of this encoding got
-- wrong).  Regulation 4: the Registrar "shall not give a licence for which a fee was fixed ... unless ... paid the fee in
-- full"; 2(d) fixes NIS 398 for the application for the temporary licence.  Taken: that fee binds the grant, so asked
-- about the GRANT the answer is the same as asked about the application.  No text prices the grant itself (s.59 lists
-- it as a separate head), and the printed lookup still says so.
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vM `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 0 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vM `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 0 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vM `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 397 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vM `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 398 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vM `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 400 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY
-- As amended, nothing paid: not free, with no index reading supplied (the updated figure is not needed to say that a payer
-- who paid nothing has not paid in full).
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vA `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vA `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) EMPTY
-- As amended, something paid: the updated figure decides.  398 x 1.0125 = 402.975 -> 403 on 4.5.2026 (the illustrative readings
-- above); 402 is not in full, 403 is; with no readings the answer for a payer who paid something is a refusal.
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vA `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 402 (YMD 2026 6 1) (`the illustrative readings`)
#ASSERT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vA `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 403 (YMD 2026 6 1) (`the illustrative readings`)
#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vA `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 402 (YMD 2026 6 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "regulation 3(a) needs the index of a month, and no reading for that month was supplied"
-- The application and the grant answer alike on the same facts.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vM `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` 398 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vA `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) EMPTY

-- Which service's fee regulation 4 looks at: for the grant of a temporary licence, the application's (taken) or its own
-- (alternative); every other service looks at its own.
#ASSERT `the service whose fee regulation 4 looks at, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, the service` `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` EQUALS `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal`
#ASSERT `the service whose fee regulation 4 looks at, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that binds a temporary licence only by a fee fixed for the licence`) `, the service` `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` EQUALS `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence`
#ASSERT `the service whose fee regulation 4 looks at, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, the service` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` EQUALS `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal`
#ASSERT `the service whose fee regulation 4 looks at, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, the service` `the service of sitting a practical exam` EQUALS `the service of sitting a practical exam`
#ASSERT `the service whose fee regulation 4 looks at, reading regulation 4 as` r4 `, the service` `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal` EQUALS `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal`

-- Alternative (only a fee fixed for the licence itself binds its grant): no text fixes one, so the grant is free whatever
-- was paid, as the first version of this encoding answered.
-- (The exported test always takes the reading the encoding takes, so the alternative is asked of `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as`.)
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that binds a temporary licence only by a fee fixed for the licence`) `, in` vM `for the service` `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` `, the payer having paid` 0 `on the day` (YMD 2025 8 1) `, under` (taken EMPTY)

-- The draft's regulation 4 is not visible: the grant answers the refusal too.
#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` vD `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 0 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "the SimpLEX draft's regulation 4 is not visible in the screenshot"

§§ `Nothing paid: no index reading is needed to bar a fee that is fixed (taken); the alternative needs the updated figure`

-- A payer who paid nothing has not paid in full a fee fixed at a positive figure.  Taken: the bar applies without the
-- updated figure, so with no readings an unpaid practical exam on 1.1.2026 is barred; paying 1 needs the figure.
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a practical exam` 0 (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a practical exam` 1 (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY BECAUSE "regulation 3(a) needs the index of a month, and no reading for that month was supplied"
-- Alternative: the updated figure decides even where nothing was paid.
#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that needs the updated figure even where nothing was paid`) `, in` vM `for the service` `the service of sitting a practical exam` `, the payer having paid` 0 `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken EMPTY) BECAUSE "regulation 3(a) needs the index of a month, and no reading for that month was supplied"
#ASSERT `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that needs the updated figure even where nothing was paid`) `, in` vM `for the service` `the service of sitting a practical exam` `, the payer having paid` 0 `on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, under` (taken (`the illustrative readings`))
-- Before the first update day nothing needs updating, and the two readings agree.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 bars the service, reading regulation 4 as` (`the reading of regulation 4 that needs the updated figure even where nothing was paid`) `, in` vM `for the service` `the service of sitting a practical exam` `, the payer having paid` 0 `on the day` (YMD 2025 12 31) `, under` (taken EMPTY)
-- A service the vintage does not price is not engaged, nothing paid or not, with or without readings.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vM `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 0 (YMD 2026 1 1) EMPTY
-- Not yet in force: no fee is fixed under the amended text on 3.5.2026, so nothing bars the grant.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vA `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 0 (YMD 2026 5 3) EMPTY

§§ `The draft: regulation 4 is not visible`

#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vD `the service of sitting a practical exam` 194 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY BECAUSE "the SimpLEX draft's regulation 4 is not visible in the screenshot"
#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vD `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 0 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY BECAUSE "the SimpLEX draft's regulation 4 is not visible in the screenshot"
#ASSERT REFUSED `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` vD `the service of attending a continuing training course` 0 (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY BECAUSE "the SimpLEX draft's regulation 4 is not visible in the screenshot"

§§ `The prohibitions themselves, exercised by trace`

-- A DEONTIC cannot be compared; the booleans above carry the assertions, and the traces below exercise the rules.
GIVETH A `Facts regulation 4 asks about`
`a fee fixed and not paid in full` MEANS
    `Facts regulation 4 asks about` WITH
        `a fee was fixed under the regulations for it` IS TRUE
        `the payer paid the fee in full` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts regulation 4 asks about`
`a fee fixed and paid in full` MEANS
    `Facts regulation 4 asks about` WITH
        `a fee was fixed under the regulations for it` IS TRUE
        `the payer paid the fee in full` IS TRUE

GIVETH A `Facts regulation 4 asks about`
`no fee fixed` MEANS
    `Facts regulation 4 asks about` WITH
        `a fee was fixed under the regulations for it` IS FALSE
        `the payer paid the fee in full` IS TRUE

-- The bar, on the three fact patterns.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 — the bar applies to the service` (`a fee fixed and not paid in full`)
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 — the bar applies to the service` (`a fee fixed and paid in full`)
#ASSERT NOT `regulation 4 — the bar applies to the service` (`no fee fixed`)

-- Expected: the Registrar gives the licence although the fee is unpaid: a breach.
#TRACE `regulation 4 — the Registrar and giving the licence` (`a fee fixed and not paid in full`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `give a licence for which a fee was fixed` AT 5
-- Expected: the same act with the fee paid in full: nothing is prohibited, FULFILLED.
#TRACE `regulation 4 — the Registrar and giving the licence` (`a fee fixed and paid in full`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `give a licence for which a fee was fixed` AT 5
-- Expected: the Registrar renews although the fee is unpaid: a breach.
#TRACE `regulation 4 — the Registrar and renewing the licence` (`a fee fixed and not paid in full`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `renew a licence for which a fee was fixed` AT 5
-- Expected: the Training Division allows the exam although the fee is unpaid: a breach.
#TRACE `regulation 4 — the Training Division and allowing the exam` (`a fee fixed and not paid in full`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Training Division` DOES `allow the performance of an exam for which a fee was fixed` AT 5
-- Expected: the Training Division allows the lodging of an objection although the fee is unpaid: a breach.
#TRACE `regulation 4 — the Training Division and allowing the objection` (`a fee fixed and not paid in full`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Training Division` DOES `allow the lodging of an objection for which a fee was fixed` AT 5
-- Expected: with no event, the prohibition stands and is printed back (no breach is reported).
#TRACE `regulation 4 — the Registrar and giving the licence` (`a fee fixed and not paid in full`) AT 0 WITH
    -- no events
-- Expected: where no fee is fixed, the bar is not engaged and the rule is FULFILLED outright.
#TRACE `regulation 4 — the Training Division and allowing the exam` (`no fee fixed`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Training Division` DOES `allow the performance of an exam for which a fee was fixed` AT 5

-- Regulation 3(b): the Director General's duty to publish the changed text, which the text gives no time for.
-- Expected: published at day 40, in time, since there is no deadline: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `regulation 3(b) — the Director General publishes the text of regulation 2 as changed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Director General of the Ministry of Labour` DOES `publish in Reshumot the text of regulation 2 as changed by the update` AT 40
-- Expected: no event: the duty stands, undated, and is printed back.
#TRACE `regulation 3(b) — the Director General publishes the text of regulation 2 as changed` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 900)
